WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.649 --> 00:00:08.210
Varys: The Maesters tell us that Aegon came
to Westeros with fire and blood, and hammered

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.380
six kingdoms into one.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:16.670
The fire he undoubtedly brought, as the Kings
of the Rock, Reach, and Iron Islands learned.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:22.580
Aegon's own son, Maegor the Cruel, was killed
by the very Iron Throne his father had forged

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.769
if you believe the tales.

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:29.760
If you don't, then perhaps "the Cruel" is
not a wise name for a king to earn.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.840
Daeron, First of His Name, tried to finish
his ancestors' work and bring Dorne into the

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.840
fold.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:42.380
For his efforts, he lost sixty thousand men
and his own life of eighteen years.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.330
During the great Targaryen civil war known
as "the Dance of the Dragons," a king and

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:53.520
queen each vied for the throne, dividing their
house and its dragons against each other.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.410
By the war's end, King's Landing was smashed,
cities razed and sacked never to be rebuilt,

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.650
and dragons had faded from this world.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:06.800
Jaime Lannister:For centuries, the Kingsguard
have been the glory of the realm.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.330
Aegon the Conqueror had established the order
as his personal guardians after uniting Westeros

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.030
with fire and blood.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.220
He knew that some of his subjects wouldn't
take to conquest, and his dragons were no

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.659
use against knives in the dark.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:24.330
No doubt surrounding himself with the greatest
knights in Westeros made his rule more palatable

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.240
and less foreign as well.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.190
Everyone in his kingdoms soon knew the names
and some of the songs of the Kingsguard.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.890
I certainly did from earliest days.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:38.740
Bronn: There was one Kingsguard (I forgot
the bastard's name) who swore an oath to his

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.420
dying Targaryen king to crown his daughter
after him.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.180
The very night that king died, this Kingsguard
crowned the king's son instead.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:52.110
When an old man on the small council dared
to protest, this honorable knight opened his

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.110
throat.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:57.340
The bastard died in the very civil war he
started along with the old king's son, daughter,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.010
and most of their dragons.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.770
And the Kingsguard?

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:06.260
All that duty and honor and not enough brains
to figure out which Targaryen to give it to.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:11.060
Twin brothers even ended up on opposite sides,
died with tears on their cheeks as they cut

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.279
each other down.

00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:17.409
I suppose I should think that's tragic, but
stupid men do stupid things every day and

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:18.760
nobody cries over them.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.920
Petyr Baelish: As little more than a boy,
Ser Criston Cole replaced the legendary Ser

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.060
RyamRedwyne on the Kingsguard and soon rose
to Lord Commander.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.400
But knights only know one way to settle disputes.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.709
When Prince Aegon's father died, SerCriston
slit the throat of an advisor who objected

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.129
to Aegon's ascension over his aunt, the anointed
heir.

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:43.349
His actions so pleased the new King, Aegon,
Second of His Name, that he appointed SerCriston

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:48.049
as his Hand in the ensuing civil war called
the Dance of Dragons.

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:53.260
Neither SerCriston nor the King nor even the
Targaryen dragons would survive it.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:58.469
Viserys Targaryen: The Targaryen dynasty united
the Seven Kingdoms and lasted nearly three

00:02:58.469 --> 00:02:59.469
centuries.

00:02:59.469 --> 00:03:07.480
It was a dynasty forged in fire, sealed in
blood, and destroyed by rebellion.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:13.269
The Targaryens are blood of the dragon, descended
from the nobility of ancient Valyria, a once-mighty

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:15.269
empire in the east.

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:20.999
When the cataclysmic Doom laid waste of Valyria
and its people, the Targaryens survived, having

00:03:20.999 --> 00:03:24.639
settled in the island fortress of Dragonstone
years before.

00:03:24.639 --> 00:03:31.459
They remained there for a century until the
rise of Aegon the Conqueror.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:37.349
Instead of attempting to reclaim the eastern
lands of his ancestors, Aegon sailed west

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:43.760
for the Seven Kingdoms, his sisters Visenya
and Rhaenys at his side.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:49.120
To keep the bloodlines pure, Aegon continued
the custom of his Valyrian ancestors and took

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.769
both of his sisters to wives.

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:55.969
Together, they came ashore on the eastern
coast of Westeros.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:04:01.430
Their blazon: a dragon with three heads, representing
Aegon and his sister-wives.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:07.459
Their words: "Fire and Blood."

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:13.199
While their host was small when compared to
the armies of the Seven Kingdoms, Aegon and

00:04:13.199 --> 00:04:16.340
his sisters had a secret weapon.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.370
The last of the dragons.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:24.690
He conquered every kingdom, save Dorne, which
eventually bowed to Targaryen rule a century

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.690
later.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.960
He had the swords of his enemies melted down
by the fiery breath of his dragon, Balerion

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.550
the Black Dread, and forged into the Iron
Throne.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:41.410
The capital city of King's Landing was built
on the eastern coast, where Aegon and his

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.940
sisters first came ashore.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:48.970
And Aegon ordered the construction of a royal
castle on its highest hill, the Red Keep.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:54.120
Samwell Tarly: According to legend, House
Targaryen survived the Doom of Valyria thanks

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:59.409
to Daenys the Dreamer, who foresaw the calamity
and convinced her father to flee their homeland.

00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:01.919
It could be true.

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:04.169
The Targaryens were always a bit more.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:11.740
Viserys Targaryen:Twelve years before the
Doom, despite the sneers of his rivals, Aenar

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.000
Targaryen abandoned the capital with his family.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.710
Legends claim that his daughter foresaw the
destruction of the city in a dream.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:27.410
More likely, Aenar met with some mishap at
court and chose exile over execution.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:34.449
He and House Targaryen slinked away to a dreary,
remote, godforsaken island.

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:37.750
Forsaken no longer.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:44.990
With arts now lost to the world, we transformed
a tiny outpost into Dragonstone, a fortress

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.330
fit for the last Dragonlords.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:53.599
Then Aenar's descendants settled into it like
a tomb for their lost homeland.

00:05:53.599 --> 00:05:56.759
Until Aegon.

00:05:56.759 --> 00:06:02.759
When he looked east, he saw the past: old,
tired, dead.

00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:11.930
But when he looked west, he saw the future:
gold in the ground, gold in the fields, and

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.379
no dragons in the sky but his.

00:06:15.379 --> 00:06:21.439
He and his sisters, Rhaenys and Visenya, flew
over the great continent, ostensibly visitors

00:06:21.439 --> 00:06:23.150
to a strange land.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:29.860
But when Aegon returned, he ordered construction
of a massive table carved in the shape of

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:34.169
Westeros, with all the notable rivers and
mountains that they had seen.

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:42.850
A personal map of the Seven Kingdoms, then
ruled by seven squabbling families.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:50.050
House Durrandon held the Stormlands from their
seat at Storm's End, due south of Dragonstone.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:55.389
House Hoare of the Iron Islands had also conquered
and enslaved the Riverlands, and ruled them

00:06:55.389 --> 00:07:01.419
from Harrenhal, a monstrous castle rising
on the shore of the Gods Eye.

00:07:01.419 --> 00:07:07.490
House Stark held the frozen wasteland of the
North, the oldest, largest, and emptiest of

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:08.490
the kingdoms.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:14.560
House Lannister held the Westerlands, the
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their gold mines.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:20.070
House Gardener held the Reach, the second
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their crops.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:23.310
House Arryn held the Vale, or rather the Vale
held them.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:29.300
The mountains were impassable except through
the Bloody Gate, which had never been taken.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.990
House Martell held the deserts of Dorne, probably
because no one else wanted them.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:41.189
Together, the Seven Kingdoms made Westeros,
a realm that wasn't yet a realm, ruled by

00:07:41.189 --> 00:07:45.860
great families who didn't know what greatness
was.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.349
Aegon would teach them.

00:07:48.349 --> 00:07:53.590
With Dorne in the fold, and the Faith put
in its place, none in Westeros were left to

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.250
oppose my family, so we started opposing each
other.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:03.680
In a Dance of Dragons, a Targaryen princess
tried to steal her brother's throne.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:07.100
Thanks to her stupidity, most of our dragons
died.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:12.270
Varys: In its time, the Dragonpit was a marvel
of the world.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:18.389
Full-grown Targaryen dragons nested beneath
its massive dome, and even on the darkest

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:23.199
nights, the walls seemed to glow with the
fire of the great beasts inside.

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:30.979
Qyburn: As had the site's previous occupant,
the Sept of Remembrance, when Maegor the Cruel

00:08:30.979 --> 00:08:34.099
blasted it with dragonfire during morning
prayers.

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:39.530
The screams of the dying men echoed through
King's Landing all day, and a pall of ash

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:42.400
and smoke hung over the city for a week.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:48.880
Varys: But as it dissipated, so too did the
rebellion of the Faith Militant.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:54.470
The Sept of Remembrance faded from memory,
and Maegor decided to replace a monument to

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:59.340
the gods with a monument to his family: the
Dragonpit.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:03.640
For more than a century, the Targaryens housed
their dragons in the Dragonpit.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.310
But dragons are not horses to be stabled or
hounds to be kenneled.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:13.210
With each generation, the dragons became less.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:16.880
Less massive, less swift, less long-lived.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.350
Qyburn: And less invulnerable.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:26.450
During the Dance of Dragons, two Targaryen
factions killed a handful of their family's

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.970
dragons while fighting each other.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:34.690
A frenzied mob even broke into the Dragonpit
and slaughtered the five dragons chained there,

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:41.480
though the last managed to bring down the
roof of the great dome on its assailants.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.670
The dragons never recovered their former strength
or numbers.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:53.760
Perhaps their line had been too broken, or
perhaps others intervened to break it further.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:59.340
But the last dragon grew no larger than a
cat, and its death earned Aegon, Third of

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:08.210
His Name, the epithet "Dragonbane."

